-- Accident Compensation Act 2001 — TESTS.
-- Expected values are worked from ../source/ACC2001.txt, not from the code.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN o IS AN Occurrence, h IS A Harm, c IS A Cause, d IS A DATE, nz IS A BOOLEAN, resident IS A BOOLEAN, ship IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Injury facts`
`injury` o h c d nz resident ship MEANS `Injury facts` OF o, h, c, d, nz, resident, ship, FALSE, FALSE

`a fall` MEANS `(a) a specific event with an external force, a sudden avoiding movement, or a twist`

`no treatment` MEANS `Treatment facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN business IS A BOOLEAN, ordinary IS A BOOLEAN, underlying IS A BOOLEAN, resource IS A BOOLEAN, consent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Treatment facts`
`treatment` business ordinary underlying resource consent MEANS `Treatment facts` OF business, ordinary, underlying, resource, consent, FALSE

`earnings of 1000 then 900` MEANS `Earnings facts` OF 4000, 4, 46800, 52, TRUE, 800, 0

GIVEN spouses IS A NUMBER, children IS A NUMBER, others IS A NUMBER, orphan IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Survivor facts`
`survivors` spouses children others orphan MEANS `Survivor facts` OF spouses, children, others, orphan

§§ `Goal 1 — accident and personal injury`

